+# Pinned versions for CI (Python 3.11, Linux x86_64): the environment the test suite was
+# last verified with. Constraints, not requirements: pyproject.toml still decides what is
+# installed; this file only decides which versions. Without it every CI run resolved the
+# newest releases, and two runs an hour apart could test different dependencies.
+# Regenerate deliberately, in a fresh Python 3.11 venv, and commit the result:
+#   pip install -e ".[api,db,postgres,redis,llm,dev]" && pip freeze --exclude-editable
